WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.760
Have you ever sent a letter to&nbsp;
someone living in another country?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.040
Have you ever ordered online a small item&nbsp;
that was sent from overseas? If you have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.560
you have experienced the benefits of the Universal&nbsp;
Postal Union. The UPU was established by treaty in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.560
1874 to help coordinate the delivery of mail&nbsp;
and parcels under 4.4 pounds between nations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.000
The UPU has been under strain recently. In 2019,&nbsp;
then president Donald Trump threatened to pull&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.600
the US out of the UPU. He was aggrieved that&nbsp;
the UPU scheme of postage rates and fees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.400
also known as terminal dues, subsidized the&nbsp;
shipment of packages from China, which they did.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.800
Ultimately, the UPU agreed to allow America and&nbsp;
other nations to increase their terminal dues. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.880
any time any nation feels it is bearing more costs&nbsp;
than benefits, it might quit the treaty. The UPU&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.520
should adjust its fees and dues more frequently,&nbsp;
and in consultation with private shipping and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:02.800
delivery firms, to better match shifting market&nbsp;
realities. Better pricing and fewer subsidies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:09.680
can keep the UPU viable in the 21st century. Have&nbsp;
you ever sent an international piece of mail or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.480
package? Let us know in our poll. Also let us&nbsp;
know what other topics you'd like our scholars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:20.240
to cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and&nbsp;
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

